--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/merge-gate.py:81` classes a merge request as bookkeeping when it only
touches `tickets/*.erg`, `tickets/closed/*.erg`, `STATE.md` or `memory/`. A
bookkeeping request gets mechanical checks only: no gaze, no verify-gate, no
review seat (`skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers). The tiering is a path
match, which is the safe part: no model judges it.

The hole is what the list holds. `AGENTS.md:21` has every session read
`memory/MEMORY.md` at task start, and `memory/topics/` carries the notes it
points to. An agent that rewrites one changes later sessions' behaviour, and
the change merges unreviewed. The threat is agent error in a single-author
repo, not an outside attacker.

Ticket bodies have the same shape (a rewritten exit criterion merges
unreviewed, then a hunt executes it), but no path can separate a body edit
from a log line; that needs a content-aware tier and is left out unless it is
observed (Option C in the hunt-simplification session, 2026-10-26).

## What to do

Remove `memory/MEMORY.md` and `memory/topics/` from bookkeeping; keep
`memory/journal/`, `memory/evidence/` and the rest of `memory/` as records.
Update the path list in `skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers to match.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/merge-gate.py` (`BOOKKEEPING`)
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers
- the merge-gate tier tests under `tests/`

## Test

`merge-gate.py tier` answers 1 (full) for a diff touching only
`memory/MEMORY.md`, 1 for one under `memory/topics/`, and still 0 for one under
`memory/journal/`.

## Exit criteria

- A diff touching `memory/MEMORY.md` or `memory/topics/` reads full tier.
- Journal and evidence edits still read bookkeeping.
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers lists the same paths as the script.
